## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to reason about crash safety, non-volatile memory semantics, and low-level ordering. Requires explicit use of durable writes, recovery procedures, and a practical benchmark plan.

## Key Concepts

- Crash-consistency and redo-logs
- Durable writes: clwb/flushopt, sfence
- Per-slot sequencing and tail/head management
- Recovery replay and correctness guarantees

## Code Example

```pseudo
structure Slot { payload; header; seq; }
function Enqueue(buf, item): void {
  Slot s = select_next_slot();
  s.payload = item;
  s.header = make_header(++tail_seq);
  persist(s.header); // clwb/flushopt + sfence
  fence();
  tail = tail + 1; // release store
}
function Dequeue(): Item {
  if (head == tail) return EMPTY;
  Item it = read_slot(head);
  head = head + 1; // release
  persist(head);
  return it;
}
```

